a stub carries no provenance (source, date, supersession). Expand (aswritten_expand with the IRIs you need) before any claim that turns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nThis entry is BOUNDED — the whole graph is deliberately not inlined. Every node is reachable within a bounded number of expands: before concluding the perspective is silent on your subject, check the map and coverage, then expand the door whose axis would hold it (^Thematic for topics and areas, ^People for anyone, ^Documents for a call or memory, ^Unplaced for loose positions). Absence becomes signal only after the relevant door shows nothing.\n\n# The map — this graph's richest ground (top fidelity band)\n\n## ^Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning  [4 children · 20260310]\nTanya frames the product against Slack's real-time model. The anti-Slack label is the primary positioning thesis: every conversation should produce a persistent decision artifact.\n  decisions-under 1 · evidence 4 — expand ^Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning for the full child index\n\n# Coverage — narrated, from four directions\n\nActive: [ Position_ContextPreservationNextSprint · Next sprint focus: context preservation — linking decisions to t… ^Position_ContextPreservationNextSprint ] · [ Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat · Real-time chat (Slack, Teams) is the named anti-pattern. The pro… ^Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat ] — the newest witnessed work, one document each.\n\n# Doors — pick an axis\n\n[ ^Thematic — every area (0) by name ] [ ^People 0 ] [ ^Dimensions — 0 axes ] [ ^Documents 2 ] [ ^Unplaced 0 ]\nEach door expands to a complete axis: aswritten_expand(iris=[\"Thematic\"]) — same coords as this perspective. Nothing in the graph is outside every door.\n\n# Focus: Testing that an omitted ref creates a topic branch; default ref behavior test by Tanya TeamOwner (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### Position_Sprint4ThesisProven\ntype: Position\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\nTanya: 'This sprint proved the thesis.' The widget intercepts the moment of consensus in any chat thread and creates a persistent decision record with full context, requiring zero extra steps.\nunder: PositioningThesis, Narrative_ZeroEffortCapture\n\n### Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning\ntype: Narrative\nwitnessed: 20260310\nsource: Sample_TeamworkProductVision_20260310\nTanya frames the product against Slack's real-time model. The anti-Slack label is the primary positioning thesis: every conversation should produce a persistent decision artifact.\nTeamwork Inc positions itself as the anti-Slack: structured async decisions over real-time noise\nunder: PositioningThesis\n\n### Obs_TanyaAntiSlackQuote\ntype: Observation\nwitnessed: 20260310\nsource: Sample_TeamworkProductVision_20260310\nTanya's verbatim framing of the anti-Slack positioning thesis.\nunder: PositioningThesis\n\n### Position_WebhookArchitecture\ntype: Position\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\nArchitecture decision: event-driven capture via webhook, not polling. Tanya: 'Polling would kill us at scale. Webhooks mean we only process actual decisions, not every message.'\nunder: StackOverview, Narrative_ZeroEffortCapture\n\n### StyleObs_Sprint4_DirectQuote\ntype: StyleObservation\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\ntrue\nDocument uses direct first-person quotes from named executives (Tanya, Tina) to anchor every key decision. Quotes are attributed inline with speaker name and colon.\n> \"This sprint proved the thesis. The widget intercepts the moment someone says 'let's go with option B'\"\nunder: ToneDirectPersonal\n\n### Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\ntype: Sample\nwitnessed: 20260322\nSprint retrospective for the async decision widget feature. Participants: Tanya Owner (CEO), Tina Teammate (Head of Product), Dev Team. Covers shipped feature, key decisions, and blockers resolved.\nSprint 4 Retro: Async Decision Widget\n\n### Obs_TanyaThesisProven\ntype: Observation\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\nTanya confirms the product thesis is validated by Sprint 4 delivery: zero-extra-step decision capture at the moment of consensus.\nunder: PositioningThesis\n\n### Sample_TeamworkProductVision_20260310\ntype: Sample\nwitnessed: 20260310\nProduct vision alignment session between Tanya Owner (CEO) and Tina Teammate (Head of Product). Establishes anti-Slack positioning, decision capture core feature, target market, and pricing.\nTeamwork Inc Product Vision\n","positions":"","pin":"f55bedc2fa045d37a849f7fb0e928eba2225e794","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":5224},"live_run_id":"8b1f89366db6","at":"2026-10-12T09:46:27Z"}
